00:18:12.464 --> 00:18:14.167
What's going on?
They're going to pay us.


00:18:14.202 --> 00:18:16.268
We have a $16 million deal
with US Robotics.


00:18:16.303 --> 00:18:18.732
-Yeah, so, uh, you guys are
getting fucked.


00:18:18.767 --> 00:18:21.702
-Why would you -- why do you
think -- why do you say that?


00:18:21.737 --> 00:18:23.605
-Well, because I would
do the same thing.


00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.409
Little operation like yours.


00:18:25.444 --> 00:18:26.905
They know they can
withhold payment


00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:29.215
till the last possible second
and then crush you.


00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:31.580
These guys, they're...
They're pirates.


00:18:31.615 --> 00:18:33.318
-Uh-huh...


00:18:35.256 --> 00:18:39.489
-We got it. Thank you.
Um...


00:18:39.524 --> 00:18:41.458
How do you know anything --


00:18:41.493 --> 00:18:44.824
What the fuck do I care?
How much money do you got?


00:18:50.634 --> 00:18:52.766
-Yeah, um...


00:18:52.801 --> 00:18:54.504
-Okay, guys?


00:18:54.539 --> 00:18:56.605
-2.50?
-Here's what I'm going to do.


00:18:56.640 --> 00:19:00.213
I will give you
$20,000 cash today.


00:19:00.248 --> 00:19:03.249
I'll sell the phone, I'll work
out this problem with USR.


00:19:03.284 --> 00:19:07.781
But I want 50% of the company,
and I've got to be CEO.


00:19:12.755 --> 00:19:14.722
-That's...
-Are you joking?


00:19:14.757 --> 00:19:17.890
No. Obviously. Obviously.
No. No!


00:19:17.925 --> 00:19:19.958
-Should I just --
-Mike?


00:19:19.993 --> 00:19:22.796
-Okay. Okay.
-Who is in charge here?


00:19:22.831 --> 00:19:24.732
-Oh, I mean, technically --
-Mike is in charge,


00:19:24.767 --> 00:19:26.470
and he says no.


00:19:32.742 --> 00:19:35.347
-I am in charge.


00:19:35.382 --> 00:19:37.877
And I say...


00:19:37.912 --> 00:19:39.813
-Sorry.


00:19:39.848 --> 00:19:41.650
-You don't need to do
what this guy says.


00:19:41.685 --> 00:19:43.289
We just met him.
He's not your dad!


00:19:43.324 --> 00:19:44.455
-Okay...


00:19:50.364 --> 00:19:53.629
-Thanks. Thank you.


00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.965
-Very sassy man.


00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.406
Wouldn't you say?


00:20:01.441 --> 00:20:05.036
He had a --
He had a sass.


00:20:05.071 --> 00:20:07.313
-"Modems, ever heard of those,"
or whatever, like --


00:20:07.348 --> 00:20:10.415
-Oh, no. I sassed him too,
but he sassed me back.


00:20:12.419 --> 00:20:16.520
Like, what's he trying to say?
We don't have our modem deal?


00:20:24.629 --> 00:20:26.827
<i>-US Robotics.</i>
<i>How may I direct your call?</i>


00:20:26.862 --> 00:20:28.829
-Yeah, it's Mike Lazaridis
from Research in Motion.


00:20:28.864 --> 00:20:30.699
We're actually building
some circuit boards


00:20:30.734 --> 00:20:32.371
for you guys.
<i>-One moment please.</i>


00:20:39.578 --> 00:20:42.414
<i>-Mike! Is that you?</i>
-Yes, hi.


00:20:42.449 --> 00:20:46.616
I was just wondering if --
if it would all --


00:20:46.651 --> 00:20:51.016
be at all possible for us to
invoice you


00:20:51.051 --> 00:20:53.854
for the first half or third


00:20:53.889 --> 00:20:57.495
of our -- your order
from us, if -- if --


00:20:57.530 --> 00:21:01.433
can -- can we invoice you
for some some of our --


00:21:01.468 --> 00:21:05.965
your order.
<i>- Oh, what?</i>


00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.033
<i>What?</i>
-If that's okay?


00:21:08.068 --> 00:21:10.068
<i>-Did you not get my fax?</i>


00:21:10.103 --> 00:21:12.774
-We don't have a fax machine.


00:21:12.809 --> 00:21:17.647
<i>-Mike, those modems</i>
<i>you sent us back in March,</i>


00:21:17.682 --> 00:21:21.453
<i>they were defective.</i>
-I'm sorry. What?


00:21:21.488 --> 00:21:23.653
<i>-Yeah, they didn't work.</i>


00:21:23.688 --> 00:21:25.391
<i>We had to cancel</i>
<i>the whole order.</i>


00:21:25.426 --> 00:21:27.591
<i>But this was months ago, buddy.</i>


00:21:29.056 --> 00:21:31.727
<i>I really thought you guys</i>
<i>had a fax machine.</i>


00:21:31.762 --> 00:21:34.895
<i>Hey, I tell you what, why don't</i>
<i>you let me make it up to you?</i>


00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:38.096
<i>I'll have USR send you one</i>
<i>free of charge on me. Okay?</i>


00:21:38.131 --> 00:21:41.539
-Um... Yeah. Okay. Thanks.


00:21:41.574 --> 00:21:44.509
<i>-Great. Okay, well,</i>
<i>good luck, Mike.</i>


00:21:44.544 --> 00:21:46.445
-Yeah.
<i>-Bye-bye.</i>


00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:47.512
-Bye.


00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:06.465
-What?


00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:09.094
Here's what you got to do:
You got to call him back,


00:22:09.129 --> 00:22:10.667
you got to
"Glengarry Glen Ross" this guy.


00:22:10.702 --> 00:22:13.406
You got to grind him.


00:22:13.441 --> 00:22:16.101
-Yeah...
I don't think I can grind him.


00:22:16.136 --> 00:22:17.707
-This is exactly what that
Rolex guy said


00:22:17.742 --> 00:22:19.445
was going to happen, right?


00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:21.073
He predicted it!
What did he say?


00:22:21.108 --> 00:22:23.878
He said US Robotics are pirates.


00:22:23.913 --> 00:22:26.144
He was fucking dead on.


00:22:26.179 --> 00:22:27.981
-Yeah.


00:22:31.118 --> 00:22:34.625
All right.


00:22:36.464 --> 00:22:38.563
-Hey, Steve? Steve?
-Yeah?


00:22:38.598 --> 00:22:40.191
-I need the phone line.


00:22:40.226 --> 00:22:44.162
-Some guy is trying to say
Noonian Soong is a Q.


00:22:44.197 --> 00:22:45.603
-Thank -- yep, thanks.


00:22:45.638 --> 00:22:47.638
-All right.
-What are you doing?


00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:53.974
-I think we should
take this deal.


00:22:54.009 --> 00:22:55.448
-No!


00:22:55.483 --> 00:22:56.614
No --


00:22:56.649 --> 00:22:58.110
So...


00:22:58.145 --> 00:23:00.211
You don't get into business
with people like this.


00:23:00.246 --> 00:23:03.181
That guy is sketchy.
-I think he's...


00:23:03.216 --> 00:23:05.722
I don't think he's sketchy.


00:23:05.757 --> 00:23:10.826
-His business card
is literally sketched out.


00:23:14.194 --> 00:23:16.194
The guy's a shark.


00:23:16.229 --> 00:23:17.899
-Okay. Do you know...


00:23:17.934 --> 00:23:20.770
Do you know who's
afraid of sharks?


00:23:22.774 --> 00:23:24.543
Pirates.


00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.983
Um, so, uh...


00:23:37.690 --> 00:23:42.924
We've been talking here,
and we --


00:23:42.959 --> 00:23:45.058
We would like to make
a counteroffer.


00:23:45.093 --> 00:23:48.963
-You came crawling back
like bugs, like grubs.


00:23:48.998 --> 00:23:55.200
-Yeah. So, we would like
to offer you...


00:23:55.235 --> 00:23:58.940
10% for...


00:23:58.975 --> 00:24:01.008
$500,000.


00:24:01.043 --> 00:24:02.680
-Are you out
of your fucking mind?!


00:24:02.715 --> 00:24:04.550
I look at 100,000 deals a day!


00:24:04.585 --> 00:24:06.244
I pick one!
Is that the quote?


00:24:06.279 --> 00:24:10.721
No. I look at 100 deals a day!
I pick one! "Wall Street."


00:24:10.756 --> 00:24:15.759
-Okay, uh, w--
uh...


00:24:15.794 --> 00:24:18.564
25% for $250,000.


00:24:18.599 --> 00:24:20.731
-50% for 50 bucks!


00:24:20.766 --> 00:24:24.295
-33% for $125,000,


00:24:24.330 --> 00:24:27.573
and you can
run the company with me.


00:24:27.608 --> 00:24:31.170
-Mike? No! No!
Yes. Deal. Deal.


00:24:31.205 --> 00:24:34.008
-Okay.
-Easy. Dude.


00:24:37.948 --> 00:24:40.685
It's going to be
totally fine.


00:24:40.720 --> 00:24:44.623
You're going to negotiate
this guy to death.


00:24:54.602 --> 00:24:56.701
<i>-Score!</i>


00:25:04.304 --> 00:25:05.809
-Yeah?
-Hi, Jim.


00:25:05.844 --> 00:25:08.713
It's Mike Lazaridis
from Research in Motion.


00:25:08.748 --> 00:25:11.012
We met at the office
the other day.


00:25:19.660 --> 00:25:23.596
So, we'd like
to offer you...


00:25:23.631 --> 00:25:27.259
33% of our company for $125,000,


00:25:27.294 --> 00:25:31.131
and you and I would be co-CEOs.


00:25:33.707 --> 00:25:35.773
<i>-...period.</i>
<i>Couple of them are suspect.</i>


00:25:35.808 --> 00:25:38.336
<i>That's their eighth shot of</i>
<i>this hockey game in 6:44.</i>


00:25:38.371 --> 00:25:40.712
-Sure.
<i>-That's an improvement.</i>


00:25:50.284 --> 00:25:52.086
-Deal.


00:25:55.223 --> 00:25:58.092
-Awesome!
Awesome! Dude!


00:25:58.127 --> 00:26:02.327
Mike! Scott! Scott?
He did it!


00:26:02.362 --> 00:26:03.999
-What do you mean?


00:26:04.034 --> 00:26:05.737
-Have you not heard anything
that's been going on


00:26:05.772 --> 00:26:07.838
in this room?


00:26:30.863 --> 00:26:32.291
-You can have,
like, two minutes


00:26:32.326 --> 00:26:35.030
-Maybe you should tell them
about the modems.


00:26:39.003 --> 00:26:43.038
-Oh, where do you want to
put him?


00:26:45.207 --> 00:26:48.340
-What the fuck is this?


00:26:48.375 --> 00:26:50.342
-That's a -- yeah,
everyone builds their own desk.


00:26:50.377 --> 00:26:53.851
That's -- that's a tradition.
-Yeah, I'm not doing that.


00:26:53.886 --> 00:26:57.756
-US Robotics pulled
out of the deal.


00:26:57.791 --> 00:27:00.055
-Told you.
What's our exposure?


00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:02.794
-Exposure?
-How much money


00:27:02.829 --> 00:27:04.191
did you spend on the modems?


00:27:04.226 --> 00:27:06.732
-Oh, $1.6 million.


00:27:06.767 --> 00:27:10.032
-One point what?!
-What?!


00:27:10.067 --> 00:27:12.837
-Spent $1.6 million
on materials and labor.


00:27:12.872 --> 00:27:16.203
-Where did you get $1.6 million?


00:27:16.238 --> 00:27:19.107
-I got a loan
from the Bank of Montreal.


00:27:19.142 --> 00:27:20.878
-Mike, come on.


00:27:20.913 --> 00:27:23.111
-Get me US Robotics!


00:27:28.756 --> 00:27:30.481
-S-- Sorry,
who are you talking to?


00:27:30.516 --> 00:27:32.791
-Yeah.


00:27:32.826 --> 00:27:34.925
-What the fuck is that?


00:27:34.960 --> 00:27:39.193
-Oh, it's called a carrier wave.
The calling modem is a --


00:27:44.299 --> 00:27:48.334
-Hey! Get off
the fucking Internet!


00:27:53.473 --> 00:27:56.045
-Yeah.
-Mike?


00:27:56.080 --> 00:28:00.478
-I think it's Casey.
-Uh-huh.


00:28:00.513 --> 00:28:05.054
-It's going to be fine, no,
it's going to be fine.


00:28:07.993 --> 00:28:09.927
You don't get to talk
to our team like that.


00:28:09.962 --> 00:28:11.797
You just get to talk -
<i>-Mike!</i>


00:28:11.832 --> 00:28:14.129
-Hi. Actually, no.
This is Jim Balsillie.


00:28:14.164 --> 00:28:16.329
I'm the CEO here now.
-Co-CEO.


00:28:16.364 --> 00:28:18.969
<i>-Okay, Jim,</i>
<i>what can I do for you?</i>


00:28:19.004 --> 00:28:21.202
-I want to talk
about these modems.


00:28:21.237 --> 00:28:23.842
<i>-Well, there's nothing</i>
<i>to talk about, sadly --</i>


00:28:23.877 --> 00:28:26.042
<i>w-we can't accept</i>
<i>the defective product.</i>


00:28:26.077 --> 00:28:29.210
-Let's cut the bullshit here.
$2.5 million, all in,


00:28:29.245 --> 00:28:31.916
for the entire order.
<i>-Yeah. No, can't do it, Jim.</i>


00:28:31.951 --> 00:28:34.215
-Then I'll decimate it for you.
$1.6 million.


00:28:34.250 --> 00:28:37.152
And if you don't take that,
I'll turn around and sell them


00:28:37.187 --> 00:28:39.858
to Rockwell for even less.


00:28:39.893 --> 00:28:41.420
-That's negotiation.


00:28:41.455 --> 00:28:44.126
<i>-Okay, how about this?</i>
<i>We'll take the modems</i>


00:28:44.161 --> 00:28:47.096
<i>if you throw in the patent</i>
<i>on Mike's phone.</i>


00:28:51.399 --> 00:28:53.465
-What phone?


00:28:53.500 --> 00:28:55.973
<i>-I thought we weren't</i>
<i>bullshitting each other, Jim.</i>


00:28:56.008 --> 00:28:59.141
<i>We've been building our own</i>
for a year, we want M--


00:28:59.176 --> 00:29:01.110
-How long to build a prototype
of the phone?


00:29:01.145 --> 00:29:05.048
-The Pocket Link?
Yeah -- a year.


00:29:05.083 --> 00:29:07.248
-No, no, no.
A prototype, Mike.


00:29:07.283 --> 00:29:08.986
A shell
I can wave around in a meeting.


00:29:09.021 --> 00:29:10.515
It could be
a complete piece of shit.


00:29:10.550 --> 00:29:12.583
-No, it --
we're not doing that.


00:29:12.618 --> 00:29:14.992
-No, we're...
Mike's not doing that.


00:29:15.027 --> 00:29:17.357
-L-listen to me: US Robotics is
building their own phone.


00:29:17.392 --> 00:29:19.425
We are now in a race
to get this thing to market,


00:29:19.460 --> 00:29:20.899
and we are a year behind.


00:29:20.934 --> 00:29:22.263
So I don't care
what you need to do.


00:29:22.298 --> 00:29:24.298
Get these fucking nerds
to drop everything


00:29:24.333 --> 00:29:27.004
and build this fucking phone!


00:29:27.039 --> 00:29:29.237
What?!


00:29:29.272 --> 00:29:32.141
-Sorry, guys, um...


00:29:32.176 --> 00:29:34.407
My girlfriend tried to cash
my check this morning


00:29:34.442 --> 00:29:37.344
and it bounced, and she said


00:29:37.379 --> 00:29:39.181
I'm not supposed
to come in here -- allowed --


00:29:39.216 --> 00:29:40.886
I shouldn't come
in here anymore.


00:29:40.921 --> 00:29:44.285
And she agreed, I won't be
coming in here any longer


00:29:44.320 --> 00:29:47.321
until I'm getting paid.
-Whoa!


00:29:54.528 --> 00:29:56.330
I can fix this.


00:30:03.636 --> 00:30:05.603
-Okay, Research in Motion.


00:30:05.638 --> 00:30:10.443
It looks like your account has
exceeded its overdraft balance.


00:30:10.478 --> 00:30:14.315
-Didn't they just deposit
a check for $125,000 from me?


00:30:16.319 --> 00:30:18.121
-Yes.


00:30:23.095 --> 00:30:25.865
-Okay. All right.
Um...


00:30:29.167 --> 00:30:33.598
I have a mortgage with you guys.
Can we pull that up, please?


00:30:33.633 --> 00:30:35.974
-Spell your last name, please.


00:30:36.009 --> 00:30:39.472
-B-A-L-S-I-L-L-I-E.


00:30:39.507 --> 00:30:43.542
-"Ball-SILLY"?
-"BAHLS-lee"


00:30:43.577 --> 00:30:46.611
-Anybody gonna miss this
red chair?


00:30:46.646 --> 00:30:48.646
-No.
-You're good.


00:30:48.681 --> 00:30:52.056
-Different guys,
different piece.


00:30:54.995 --> 00:30:57.193
-All right, everybody,
listen up.


00:30:57.228 --> 00:30:59.360
From now on, checks will be
coming every two weeks.


00:30:59.395 --> 00:31:01.131
You will come get them
from Shelly.


00:31:01.166 --> 00:31:03.265
This is Shelly.
-Hi.


00:31:13.244 --> 00:31:15.343
-All right.
That's you, Shell.


00:31:17.512 --> 00:31:19.281
Mike!


00:31:22.022 --> 00:31:23.989
-Me too?
-Yeah, sure.


00:31:32.725 --> 00:31:35.429
-Sorry. Who --
So, who is Shelly?


00:31:35.464 --> 00:31:37.134
-Shelly?


00:31:37.169 --> 00:31:40.137
-Oh, dude,
that thing's haunting you.


00:31:40.172 --> 00:31:41.600
-No, I'm motivating you.


00:31:41.635 --> 00:31:44.240
And don't call me that thing.
I'm your boss.


00:31:44.275 --> 00:31:46.077
-No. No, you're not.
-Yeah?


00:31:46.112 --> 00:31:47.540
-Get me John Woodman
at Bell Atlantic.


00:31:47.575 --> 00:31:50.642
-You got it.
-Wait, um, what are you doing?


00:31:50.677 --> 00:31:54.712
-We are selling the phone.
Mike, I need a prototype.


00:31:54.747 --> 00:31:56.483
-I told you, I don't --
-Mike?


00:31:56.518 --> 00:31:58.254
<i>-Connecting you.</i>


00:31:58.289 --> 00:32:02.126
-Guys, -we are over $1 million
in debt with no assets,


00:32:02.161 --> 00:32:04.997
no contracts and no products.


00:32:05.032 --> 00:32:07.329
<i>-John Woodman's office.</i>
-Hi, this is Jim Balsillie,


00:32:07.364 --> 00:32:10.167
CEO of Research in Motion.
-Co-CEO.


00:32:10.202 --> 00:32:12.697
<i>-One moment, please.</i>


00:32:12.732 --> 00:32:15.172
Okay?
-Yeah, I --


00:32:15.207 --> 00:32:18.340
-No! He said there's no phone!
-I'm not asking you!


00:32:20.443 --> 00:32:23.444
Mike.


00:32:23.479 --> 00:32:24.775
-Okay.
-"Okay" --


00:32:24.810 --> 00:32:26.612
wh-what do you mean, okay?


00:32:26.647 --> 00:32:28.581
No, no, wait. Wait a minute.
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.


00:32:28.616 --> 00:32:30.616
Wait, wait, wait a minute.
Wait a minute.


00:32:30.651 --> 00:32:32.618
<i>-John Whitman.</i>
-Mr. Woodman, I am about


00:32:32.653 --> 00:32:34.455
to make you insanely rich.


00:32:41.365 --> 00:32:44.564
-Mike does not agree with this?
-He just fucking did!


00:32:44.599 --> 00:32:47.468
-That was duress! Okay?!
You're manipulating him!


00:32:47.503 --> 00:32:50.702
It's obvious!
What do you want me to do?


00:32:50.737 --> 00:32:52.209
-Uh...
-What?


00:32:56.677 --> 00:32:59.810
-So there's a reason
why your intercom


00:32:59.845 --> 00:33:01.647
is emitting white noise.


00:33:01.682 --> 00:33:04.419
It's because it was
manufactured in China


00:33:04.454 --> 00:33:07.092
by engineers who didn't care.


00:33:07.127 --> 00:33:09.622
And now every office
in the world


00:33:09.657 --> 00:33:12.328
has to suffer an annoying hiss,


00:33:12.363 --> 00:33:16.497
a blinking red light,
15 different power cords


00:33:16.532 --> 00:33:18.730
that are utterly incompatible
with one another.


00:33:18.765 --> 00:33:21.370
So we're not doing that.


00:33:21.405 --> 00:33:25.308
We are not just adding
to the hiss.


00:33:25.343 --> 00:33:27.475
I will build a prototype,


00:33:27.510 --> 00:33:31.677
but I'll do it perfectly
or I don't do it.


00:33:31.712 --> 00:33:33.811
-Mike, are you familiar
with the saying


00:33:33.846 --> 00:33:35.813
"perfect is the enemy of good"?


00:33:40.523 --> 00:33:44.525
-Well, good enough
is the enemy of humanity.


00:34:15.195 --> 00:34:18.493
Shelley, get John Woodman
back on, please.


00:34:18.528 --> 00:34:21.760
-So I reach out,
hang up the phone.


00:34:21.795 --> 00:34:24.466
He looks up at me like,
"Are you ready to die?"


