01:28:16.763 --> 01:28:18.730
So it's still a BlackBerry.


01:28:18.765 --> 01:28:20.699
It's our BlackBerry.
So you --


01:28:20.734 --> 01:28:22.932
Except for where --
where we have keys here,


01:28:22.967 --> 01:28:29.807
um, screen, the whole thing
is a screen, except ours,


01:28:29.842 --> 01:28:35.450
when you press it, you'll get
that that satisfying click,


01:28:35.485 --> 01:28:38.816
that BlackBerry click,
our trademark click.


01:28:38.851 --> 01:28:43.821
So, screen, keyboard, phone.


01:28:43.856 --> 01:28:47.121
Screen, keyboard, phone.


01:28:48.157 --> 01:28:52.500
Screen, keyboard, phone.


01:28:52.535 --> 01:28:54.931
Are you getting it?


01:29:10.883 --> 01:29:14.049
-Mike. Mike?
What the fuck was that, dude!


01:29:14.084 --> 01:29:15.853
-Where is this fucking limo?


01:29:15.888 --> 01:29:18.625
-Capacity max is at 17,000,
but we can enhance it


01:29:18.660 --> 01:29:20.693
to 19,000
without too much trouble.


01:29:20.728 --> 01:29:22.662
-All right. I want all this
basketball shit gone.


01:29:22.697 --> 01:29:25.830
From now on,
this place is a permanent rink.


01:29:28.769 --> 01:29:31.704
We can't do that.
-Why?


01:29:31.739 --> 01:29:33.134
-We have active contracts
with a dozen clients.


01:29:33.169 --> 01:29:35.576
-Cancel 'em.
-Yeah, but there's going to --


01:29:35.611 --> 01:29:37.039
-I'll pay the fines.


01:29:37.074 --> 01:29:41.142
I want that
to be my personal box.


01:29:41.177 --> 01:29:42.946
-That's not a box.


01:29:46.182 --> 01:29:47.918
That's not a box.


01:29:47.953 --> 01:29:49.183
-No, no, no.


01:29:49.218 --> 01:29:51.691
Okay, so it's a screen,


01:29:51.726 --> 01:29:54.628
but it needs a raised hinge
or actuator,


01:29:54.663 --> 01:29:56.630
as I wrote, between it
and the body


01:29:56.665 --> 01:29:59.864
so the entire device clicks
when you press on it.


01:30:02.066 --> 01:30:03.835
-Wait. What?


01:30:06.202 --> 01:30:08.807
-I'm just wondering why
we want to do that.


01:30:08.842 --> 01:30:11.106
-That -- that -- that --
is not the question


01:30:11.141 --> 01:30:13.647
you ask me here.
I don't --


01:30:13.682 --> 01:30:16.210
"Why" does not matter to you?
Okay?


01:30:16.245 --> 01:30:18.014
Because I said so.


01:30:18.049 --> 01:30:20.852
Because that's what I sold.
Okay?


01:30:20.887 --> 01:30:23.151
Who are you, by the way?


01:30:23.186 --> 01:30:25.659
-Easy, Mike.


01:30:25.694 --> 01:30:28.530
-Oh, come on, guys, please.


01:30:28.565 --> 01:30:30.796
Silent mode!
When we're at the office.


01:30:30.831 --> 01:30:32.534
Charles!


01:30:32.569 --> 01:30:34.800
-Phones off.
-Sorry. Sorry, Mike.


01:30:34.835 --> 01:30:35.768
Sorry, everybody.


01:30:37.805 --> 01:30:40.201
-Okay, so you know what I think
all this is,


01:30:40.236 --> 01:30:44.238
is we're trying to do the old
BlackBerry click


01:30:44.273 --> 01:30:47.516
while embracing
the new iPhone screen.


01:30:47.551 --> 01:30:48.946
That's all.
-No, no, no.


01:30:48.981 --> 01:30:52.719
We're not embracing
anything to do with Apple!


01:30:52.754 --> 01:30:56.217
Guys!


01:30:56.252 --> 01:30:58.120
It's really not hard.


01:30:58.155 --> 01:31:00.859
Okay? We pay you a lot of money.


01:31:00.894 --> 01:31:02.663
This is really not hard.


01:31:02.698 --> 01:31:06.095
It's a keyboard on a screen,


01:31:06.130 --> 01:31:07.932
on a keyboard.


01:31:12.675 --> 01:31:14.675
And I don't care
what you think of it.


01:31:14.710 --> 01:31:17.007
-Mike.


01:31:28.625 --> 01:31:29.723
Fuck is Doug talking about.


01:31:29.758 --> 01:31:31.252
Embracing what Apple is doing?


01:31:31.287 --> 01:31:32.759
I don't understand.


01:31:32.794 --> 01:31:34.024
-You come back from New York


01:31:34.059 --> 01:31:35.663
talking about
a brand new phone, right?


01:31:35.698 --> 01:31:38.699
Prototype in a week.
What are we doing here?


01:31:38.734 --> 01:31:40.030
-Can I talk to you?
-It's a prototype,


01:31:40.065 --> 01:31:41.669
Charles, I can build
the fucking thing myself


01:31:41.704 --> 01:31:43.803
in a night if I had to.
-We still got to ship


01:31:43.838 --> 01:31:46.135
the goddamn thing.
-I said use the Onyx --


01:31:46.170 --> 01:31:49.611
-I did! On curve!


01:31:56.048 --> 01:31:59.621
All right, China.


01:31:59.656 --> 01:32:01.249
It's the only way
this gets done.


01:32:01.284 --> 01:32:04.318
I'm sorry, China.


01:32:14.671 --> 01:32:18.607
-Yeah. Fuck it. Do it.


01:32:18.642 --> 01:32:20.334
China.


01:32:20.369 --> 01:32:21.973
China. Let's do it.
-Wait. No, no.


01:32:22.008 --> 01:32:23.975
He doesn't mean that.
-Hey, hey, hey. Don't --


01:32:24.010 --> 01:32:26.109
Don't speak for me.
-But, Mike, what are you doing?


01:32:26.144 --> 01:32:28.276
-What am I doing? I'm trying to
keep our biggest


01:32:28.311 --> 01:32:30.685
fucking customer, what the fuck
are you doing?


01:32:33.349 --> 01:32:35.118
-Mike, I'm trying to help you.
-You're not though.


01:32:35.153 --> 01:32:36.691
You're not.
You're not helping me.


01:32:36.726 --> 01:32:38.022
This doesn't help me.


01:32:38.057 --> 01:32:39.793
If you can help me,
we wouldn't be here.


01:32:39.828 --> 01:32:42.631
I don't need your fucking
help anymore, okay?


01:32:42.666 --> 01:32:44.259
You're fucking useless!


01:32:52.302 --> 01:32:54.104
-Okay.


01:33:04.413 --> 01:33:06.215
-Figure out China


01:33:14.258 --> 01:33:16.027
Figure out China.


01:33:17.866 --> 01:33:20.229
And I'll build
the fucking thing myself.


01:33:50.998 --> 01:33:53.295
Fuck.


01:33:53.330 --> 01:33:55.737
What?
<i>-Is this Mike Lazaridis?</i>


01:33:55.772 --> 01:33:58.300
-Who's -- Who's this?
<i>-My name is Dara Frankel.</i>


01:33:58.335 --> 01:34:01.138
<i>I'm from the SEC.</i>
<i>Do you have a second?</i>


01:34:01.173 --> 01:34:04.240
-Not really. Not right now.
What is this about?


01:34:04.275 --> 01:34:05.945
<i>-I'm trying to track down</i>
<i>some information</i>


01:34:05.980 --> 01:34:08.442
<i>on some stock options</i>
<i>your company issued.</i>


01:34:08.477 --> 01:34:11.852
-Well, that's not -- I wouldn't
know anything about that.


01:34:11.887 --> 01:34:15.185
I think you'd want
to talk to Jim.


01:34:15.220 --> 01:34:18.727
<i>-Okay.</i>
<i>Would there be a good time</i>


01:34:18.762 --> 01:34:21.356
<i>to come in and talk about this?</i>


01:34:21.391 --> 01:34:23.325
-No, I don't -- no.


01:34:26.066 --> 01:34:27.736
-Okay. I'm here.


01:34:27.771 --> 01:34:29.067
I'm here. I'm here. I'm here.


01:34:29.102 --> 01:34:30.970
-Jack Manishen says
he needs to see you.


01:34:31.005 --> 01:34:32.807
-Okay. Yeah. Where is he?


01:34:32.842 --> 01:34:36.778
-Camped outside your office.
-Great.


01:34:40.542 --> 01:34:43.411
-Shell, do me a favor.


01:34:43.446 --> 01:34:45.919
Reach out to Carl Yankowski's
office and let him know


01:34:45.954 --> 01:34:48.053
that Jim Balsillie's got
opening night tickets


01:34:48.088 --> 01:34:50.121
to the Hamilton Penguins
for him.


01:34:50.156 --> 01:34:53.025
I know how much
he loves hockey.


01:34:58.395 --> 01:35:00.362
All right, all right. Relax.
You got me.


01:35:00.397 --> 01:35:02.430
-That same woman from the SEC
keeps calling.


01:35:02.465 --> 01:35:05.136
Can I give her your number?
-No.


01:35:07.503 --> 01:35:17.115
-Okay, so first quarter,
second quarter, third quarter.


01:35:19.218 --> 01:35:22.153
Fourth quarter.


01:35:22.188 --> 01:35:23.352
And this is us.


01:35:27.127 --> 01:35:28.863
-Whose numbers are these?


01:35:28.898 --> 01:35:30.260
-Apple's internal projections.


01:35:30.295 --> 01:35:33.296
-They released the numbers
on Friday.


01:35:33.331 --> 01:35:36.134
-$500 fully subsidized?


01:35:36.169 --> 01:35:38.939
This is the most expensive
phone in the world.


01:35:38.974 --> 01:35:39.907
-It has the highest
consumer interest


01:35:39.942 --> 01:35:41.469
of any product in history.


01:35:41.504 --> 01:35:44.340
We're going to go from
number one phone in the world


01:35:44.375 --> 01:35:49.048
to that phone that people had
before they bought an iPhone.


01:35:57.124 --> 01:36:00.521
-It's gonna be fine.
Mike'll figure it out.


01:36:02.294 --> 01:36:04.327
What?


01:36:12.205 --> 01:36:14.007
-Hey, um...


01:36:16.638 --> 01:36:19.441
Why is the SEC looking at us?


01:36:19.476 --> 01:36:21.146
-They called you?


01:36:21.181 --> 01:36:24.985
-Yeah. Something --
Something about stock options?


01:36:25.020 --> 01:36:27.119
-I'm sure it's nothing. Yeah.


01:36:27.154 --> 01:36:29.550
-It -- It's nothing?


01:36:29.585 --> 01:36:32.388
-Yeah. What's with this
Apple thing?


01:36:34.326 --> 01:36:36.128
-What--What about it?


01:36:36.163 --> 01:36:39.626
-Are we worried?
-No.


01:36:39.661 --> 01:36:41.595
-Okay. Why?


01:36:41.630 --> 01:36:43.399
-Because one of them
uses as much data


01:36:43.434 --> 01:36:45.203
as 5,000 BlackBerrys.


01:36:45.238 --> 01:36:48.041
Because it has no keyboard.
Because the thing is a joke.


01:36:50.375 --> 01:36:53.475
-So why are people telling me
that they're about to kill us?


01:36:53.510 --> 01:36:55.983
-Because they're idiots.


01:37:20.240 --> 01:37:23.604
-Get me a meeting
with Stan Sigman at AT&T.


01:37:31.251 --> 01:37:34.087
-What are you doing?


01:37:35.684 --> 01:37:37.684
<i>-Okay, so the soonest</i>
<i>I can get is next month.</i>


01:37:37.719 --> 01:37:39.587
<i>His office said he's</i>
<i>leaving for vacation today.</i>


01:37:39.622 --> 01:37:42.689
-Tell him I'm coming
to Atlanta right now.


01:37:50.204 --> 01:37:52.303
Let's go. Let's go!


01:37:52.338 --> 01:37:53.667
Tell them we'll be there
in an hour.


01:37:53.702 --> 01:37:56.241
-Hey, it's --


01:37:58.740 --> 01:38:00.707
-Gary, how are you?


01:38:00.742 --> 01:38:02.313
<i>-Good. We're ready</i>
<i>to go over here.</i>


01:38:02.348 --> 01:38:04.612
<i>How soon can</i>
<i>you get to New York?</i>


01:38:06.385 --> 01:38:09.485
-Great, uh...Anytime tomorrow.


01:38:09.520 --> 01:38:12.257
<i>-How about today?</i>


01:38:12.292 --> 01:38:14.028
-That might be
a little tight for me.


01:38:14.063 --> 01:38:15.557
<i>-I've got the board here now,</i>
<i>and I don't know</i>


01:38:15.592 --> 01:38:17.427
<i>when they're all going</i>
<i>to be together again.</i>


01:38:17.462 --> 01:38:20.067
<i>-If you want to wait,</i>
<i>up to you.</i>


01:38:20.102 --> 01:38:22.366
<i>It's your deal.</i>


01:38:22.401 --> 01:38:24.731
-Yeah. No, that works, Gary.


01:38:24.766 --> 01:38:27.041
I'll -- Yeah, I'll be there.


01:38:27.076 --> 01:38:28.537
<i>-Looking forward to it.</i>


01:38:28.572 --> 01:38:30.374
-Okay. Alright. Bye.


01:38:32.477 --> 01:38:35.478
Change of plans.
We're going to JFK.


01:38:35.513 --> 01:38:37.612
-We're dialed in.


01:38:37.647 --> 01:38:39.416
-Listen to me, you mouthy fuck!


01:38:39.451 --> 01:38:42.056
If I say we're going to JFK,
we're going to JFK!


01:38:42.091 --> 01:38:43.486
Do you understand?


01:38:43.521 --> 01:38:46.258
-So we're--we're not meeting
with Sigman, then?


01:38:46.293 --> 01:38:48.524
-I'm doing it all.


01:39:30.568 --> 01:39:32.205
-Hey!


01:39:32.240 --> 01:39:33.503
Fuck.


01:39:38.345 --> 01:39:40.477
-Where's Jim?
-I have no idea.


01:39:40.512 --> 01:39:41.775
-C'mon, we got
to get you out of here.


01:39:41.810 --> 01:39:43.315
-What? Why?
-SEC is raiding us.


01:39:43.350 --> 01:39:44.514
-Wait, what?


01:39:44.549 --> 01:39:45.779
-Give me your phone.


01:39:45.814 --> 01:39:48.518
-Where's your goddamn phone?


01:39:48.553 --> 01:39:50.652
-Mike Lazaridis?


01:39:50.687 --> 01:39:53.523
-Can you handle this?


01:39:53.558 --> 01:39:56.163
Who are you?
-We spoke on the phone.


01:39:56.198 --> 01:39:58.396
You want to come and answer
some questions?


01:40:02.303 --> 01:40:04.732
-Sure. Sure.


01:40:08.243 --> 01:40:10.276
After me, is it? Okay.


01:40:11.873 --> 01:40:13.411
-Okay.


01:40:13.446 --> 01:40:14.775
-Okay, what?
What are they doing?


01:40:14.810 --> 01:40:16.348
That's -- That's -- No, no.


01:40:16.383 --> 01:40:17.844
They can't touch
any of that stuff.


01:40:17.879 --> 01:40:20.088
They --


01:40:36.271 --> 01:40:38.403
-Passwords on everything.
-Oh.


01:40:38.438 --> 01:40:41.604
What's the password, Mike?


01:40:41.639 --> 01:40:45.377
-Am I required
to give that to you?


01:40:45.412 --> 01:40:46.576
-No.


01:40:46.611 --> 01:40:50.283
Are you hiding something?


01:40:50.318 --> 01:40:51.878
-Um...


01:40:51.913 --> 01:40:56.388
Should I not have a lawyer
or something with me for this?


01:40:56.423 --> 01:40:58.489
-Do you think you need a lawyer?


01:41:14.309 --> 01:41:16.309
-Jim.


01:41:29.225 --> 01:41:30.422
-Gary, what's going on?


01:41:30.457 --> 01:41:32.490
You got me --
got me waiting out here.


01:41:32.525 --> 01:41:34.591
-Jim, look, we're not going to
waste your time here, okay?


01:41:34.626 --> 01:41:38.496
It's not going to happen
with you and the Penguins.


01:41:38.531 --> 01:41:40.234
-What?


01:41:40.269 --> 01:41:42.566
-We held a vote with the other
owners and unfortunately,


01:41:42.601 --> 01:41:45.470
it went against you, 26 to 0.


01:41:45.505 --> 01:41:47.406
-Hold on a second.
Hold on, hold on.


01:41:47.441 --> 01:41:50.244
I thought we had a deal.


01:41:50.279 --> 01:41:52.642
When did the other owners
even get...?


01:41:52.677 --> 01:41:55.249
I'm sorry.
What changed here, man?


01:41:55.284 --> 01:41:56.547
-The owners did not find you


01:41:56.582 --> 01:42:00.848
to be of good
character and integrity.


01:42:00.883 --> 01:42:04.588
-I don't know
what the hell that means.


01:42:04.623 --> 01:42:07.954
Gary, what the fuck is this?


01:42:07.989 --> 01:42:09.593
-You know, it's funny.


01:42:09.628 --> 01:42:11.232
It's one thing
to have a secret plan


01:42:11.267 --> 01:42:13.828
to fuck over the NHL
and move a team to Canada.


01:42:13.863 --> 01:42:15.566
It's another thing to brag


01:42:15.601 --> 01:42:19.405
to your rich friends before you
actually do it.


01:42:29.318 --> 01:42:32.319
-Oh, you guys are
so fucking stupid.


01:42:35.258 --> 01:42:38.556
You know what? Maybe I'll buy
this whole fucking league.


01:42:38.591 --> 01:42:39.821
Huh? How about that?


01:42:39.856 --> 01:42:41.790
-Don, can we see that
Mr. Balsillie


01:42:41.825 --> 01:42:43.462
get safely back to Canada?


01:42:43.497 --> 01:42:46.729
-Oh, fuck all you people!


01:42:46.764 --> 01:42:50.238
Fuck you!


01:42:50.273 --> 01:42:51.899
Get ready for a hostile takeover


01:42:51.934 --> 01:42:55.672
of this entire fucking league,
okay, you fuck?


01:42:55.707 --> 01:42:57.905
You think I won't fucking do it?


01:42:57.940 --> 01:43:03.581
I'm from Waterloo,
where the vampires hang out!


01:43:08.951 --> 01:43:10.522
Go, go, go, go, go!


01:43:10.557 --> 01:43:15.329
-We'll never make it.
-I said let's go!


01:43:15.364 --> 01:43:16.693
-Delay Sigman.
-I called.


01:43:16.728 --> 01:43:17.859
They said he's already left
for vacation?


01:43:17.894 --> 01:43:19.432
-Where?


01:43:19.467 --> 01:43:20.928
-They just said
he's going to the airport.


01:43:20.963 --> 01:43:22.732
-Great, so are we.


01:43:31.314 --> 01:43:34.777
-And is this your signature?


01:43:34.812 --> 01:43:37.615
-Yep.


01:43:41.555 --> 01:43:42.851
-And this?


01:43:42.886 --> 01:43:44.457
I don't know
what you're looking for.


01:43:44.492 --> 01:43:47.691
These are standard
employment contracts.


01:43:47.726 --> 01:43:51.893
-I'm just wondering how you
convinced all these engineers


01:43:51.928 --> 01:43:54.962
from around the world
to come all the way to Canada.


01:43:54.997 --> 01:43:57.701
It doesn't make sense.


01:43:57.736 --> 01:44:01.771
-It's because they get to work
on the best phone in the world.


01:44:01.806 --> 01:44:03.575
-Mike.
-Hmm?


01:44:03.610 --> 01:44:07.579
-Each of these contracts
offers backdated stock options.


01:44:07.614 --> 01:44:09.449
You were illegally pricing
your own shares


01:44:09.484 --> 01:44:13.519
so you could hire engineers
with money you didn't have.


01:44:20.528 --> 01:44:22.363
Do you know what the sentence is


01:44:22.398 --> 01:44:24.695
for multi-million dollar
stock fraud?


01:44:29.504 --> 01:44:35.035
-Okay, I swear I had no idea
about any of what you just said.


01:44:35.070 --> 01:44:37.411
-Do you expect me
to believe that?


01:44:37.446 --> 01:44:39.809
You're CEO.


01:44:51.823 --> 01:44:54.626
-Co-CEO.


01:44:54.661 --> 01:44:56.760
<i>-Tell me why this can't wait</i>
<i>another few weeks.</i>


01:44:56.795 --> 01:44:58.124
-I'm telling you, Stan.


01:44:58.159 --> 01:45:00.632
-I'm headed for the terminal
right now.


01:45:00.667 --> 01:45:02.029
<i>-What?</i>
-Well, hold on.


01:45:02.064 --> 01:45:05.835
-I'm at gate 7. Where are you?


01:45:05.870 --> 01:45:09.938
<i>-Are you running?</i>
-No, Stan. No, I'm good.


01:45:09.973 --> 01:45:13.073
I'm telling you, I'm --
just give me the gate.


01:45:13.108 --> 01:45:14.910
<i>-I'm getting</i>
<i>on a plane here, Jim.</i>


01:45:14.945 --> 01:45:17.616
-Okay, listen, Stan.


01:45:17.651 --> 01:45:20.047
Alright, here's the headline.


01:45:20.082 --> 01:45:24.458
Half a million BlackBerrys
for AT&T for $0.


01:45:24.493 --> 01:45:26.625
<i>-What's the catch?</i>
-Nope. No catch.


01:45:26.660 --> 01:45:30.398
They're yours if you're willing
to release them at a discount


01:45:30.433 --> 01:45:32.092
one month before the iPhone.


01:45:32.127 --> 01:45:35.403
<i>-</i>


01:45:35.438 --> 01:45:38.670
-Stan, come on. You owe me.


01:45:38.705 --> 01:45:40.639
You've sold a lot of minutes
because of us.


01:45:40.674 --> 01:45:42.872
<i>-Yeah, but you know</i>
<i>what the problem</i>


01:45:42.907 --> 01:45:44.940
<i>with selling minutes is?</i>


01:45:44.975 --> 01:45:46.546
-What?


01:45:46.581 --> 01:45:49.846
<i>-There's only one minute</i>
<i>in a minute.</i>


01:46:09.967 --> 01:46:11.604
<i>-Hey.</i>
-Okay, Mike, listen to me.


01:46:11.639 --> 01:46:12.803
I think we've got
a big problem here.


01:46:12.838 --> 01:46:14.167
I know what Apple's doing.


01:46:14.202 --> 01:46:15.575
<i>-We shouldn't</i>
<i>talk on the phone.</i>


01:46:15.610 --> 01:46:18.105
-Why?
-Um, we're in trouble.


01:46:18.140 --> 01:46:22.010
<i>-Why?</i>
-We're in trouble with the SEC.


01:46:22.045 --> 01:46:25.684
But get back as soon as you can.


01:46:25.719 --> 01:46:27.620
<i>I have a way</i>
<i>to get us out of this.</i>


01:47:09.125 --> 01:47:11.026
-Hey.


01:47:11.061 --> 01:47:13.699
Okay, so, listen.


01:47:13.734 --> 01:47:16.999
AT&T knows exactly
what they're doing.


01:47:17.034 --> 01:47:19.870
They wanted Apple to build them
a data-guzzling monster,


01:47:19.905 --> 01:47:21.740
because that's where they're
going to move the market.


01:47:21.775 --> 01:47:23.643
They're not selling minutes
anymore, Mike.


01:47:23.678 --> 01:47:27.042
They're selling data.


01:47:27.077 --> 01:47:32.179
-He's here.


01:47:32.214 --> 01:47:34.049
-Who's that?


01:47:35.855 --> 01:47:38.020
-They're waiting
for you next door.


01:47:40.156 --> 01:47:43.157
-Who's --


01:47:43.192 --> 01:47:46.193
What -- What did you do?


01:47:46.228 --> 01:47:47.964
-I made a deal.


01:47:47.999 --> 01:47:49.603
The SEC gets you,


01:47:49.638 --> 01:47:51.869
your board seat,
and our full cooperation


01:47:51.904 --> 01:47:54.608
in their criminal investigation.


01:47:54.643 --> 01:47:57.809
And for that,
they'll leave us alone.


01:48:04.587 --> 01:48:07.984
And they want $183 million.


01:48:38.379 --> 01:48:40.654
-You said next door?
